### Problem / Use Case

Add a built-in observability and evaluation layer for LLM usage.

The feature should support per-agent model credentials, request correlation IDs, task-type tagging, cost/token/latency tracking, tool-call success metrics, and persistent usage logs.

It should also support shadow routing: a configurable percentage of production requests are duplicated to a secondary local or alternative model for evaluation only. Shadow responses must never affect the user-facing response, execute tools, or perform external actions.

This would enable teams to compare cloud and local models on real workloads and generate reliable 30-day reports covering:

cost per agent/task/model;
latency and cold vs warm performance;
success and fallback rates;
tool-call reliability;
local-vs-cloud quality;
estimated savings;
recommended routing per task type.

The goal is to make Rakazo capable of data-driven model routing and safe migration from expensive cloud models to local or cheaper models without risking production quality.

